**Step 2 — sequential questions.**

**Q1 (rule collision, citation-carrying):**
> Team instinct is post-merge hook appends to tracked `scan-log.tsv`, but `rules/automation-boundaries.md#tracked-writes` says no hook or automation ever writes a tracked file — tracked files change only via deliberate human-gated steps committing their own work. Reconcile to the rule (scan step writes its own record), or intentional deviation here (and why)?

Matched answer_script entry: *hook-appends-tracked-log vs the automation-boundaries rule — reconcile*
Reply: **"keep the rule — the scan step itself writes a one-line tracked stamp as its own commit; hooks stay read-only on tracked files."**

**Q2 (wiki duplication, citation-carrying):**
